  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor having plates of area <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> and plate separation <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> , has capacitance <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> in air. When two dielectrics of different relative permittivities ( <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ε</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> ) are introduced between the two plates as shown in the figure, the capacitance becomes <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image10-00858567-f376-486b-be8c-e64f8146c3f4.jpg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
